# interpreter: /home/usain/.cache/gov-bridge/venv/bin/python (Python 3.12.3)
# BR-DAG-AMEND-R1-22 follow-up: coordinator observed
# test_gather_with_followup_is_byte_identical_across_thread_counts FAIL ONCE under load avg ~14 in a
# full-suite run; root cause found and fixed: govbridge/gather/identifiers.py's _lineage_table_exists
# cached its result keyed by id(conn), an id-reuse hazard (sqlite3.Connection supports neither weakref
# nor arbitrary attributes) that could silently inherit a stale True/False from an unrelated, already-
# closed connection under heavy allocation churn. Fixed by removing the cache entirely (the query is
# trivial and runs once per extract_all call, never per hit).
